## What mattered most
The visitor flagged three things only the researcher could answer. Reading the SAGE code answered all three, and the site was wrong on each:

1. **"Raising never changes weights" was false for part of the history.** From 2026-01-27 to 2026-03-06, the archived Sprout Qwen 0.5B line trained a LoRA adapter on its own raising sessions and loaded it back in. 84 of its session records say `using_lora: true`. Weights have only been frozen since SAGE's curriculum doc of 2026-04-04. This is the same line /raising uses for its main identity observation. I qualified the claim on /raising, /principles and twice on /context.
2. **The post-session "dream consolidation" step is Claude** (`claude --print`), not the entity's own model. It rewrites the identity file after every session. /raising now names it, adds the analogy caveat, and lists it as a possible explanation for vocabulary drift.
3. **"BECOMING pattern observed: creating" on all six /fleet cards was a schedule, not an observation.** The raising scripts set it from the session number (41 and up means "creating"). It is now labelled as the curriculum phase.

